<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n33177" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ostōrĭus</span></b> , i,
			m., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>the name of several Romans.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> Ostorins Sabinus, <i>a Roman knight</i>, <i><span class="en">Tac. A. 16,
				23</span></i>; <i><span class="en">16, 30</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quaestor,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 16, 33</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> P.
			Ostorius Scapula, <i>proprœtor in
			Britain</i>, <i><span class="en">Tac. A. 12, 31</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">bello egregius,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. Agr.
					14</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b> M.
			Ostorius Scapula, <i>son of Publius</i>, <i><span class="en">Tac. A. 12,
				31</span></i>; <i>put to death by Nero</i>,
					<i><span class="en">id. ib. 16</span></i>. 15.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
